    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T12:19:19Z",
    "body": "Here's the argument I was tempted to make:\n\n> There are lots of ways to use DOM APIs to produce trees that don't survive reparsing, and what we've done here is closer to the existing `element.setAttribute()`, which is nice for consistency. Those APIs are also for the XML syntax, after all.\n\nHowever, that's not a solid argument. The way that PI attributes work isn't quite like anything else, so what should it be consistent with? Moreover, both `data` and the parsed attributes are always there and in sync, and you can stumble into roundtrip issues with the seemingly innocent `pi.data += ' more=\"attributes\"'`.\n\nSo yes, I'm OK with this!",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
